course: dictionary
lesson: 138
title: Advisable: a sensible idea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Advisable is a formal word, often found in safety notices and advice. It means sensible and wise to do, or recommended. Read the example: «It is advisable to wear a helmet when you ride a bike.» The words around it show that a helmet is a good idea, even though nobody is forcing you to wear one.
explain: Context clues help. The word "advice" sits inside "advisable", so the word is about giving advice. When you meet it, swap in a simpler meaning, such as "a good idea", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In Alice's Adventures in Wonderland, the Mouse says the archbishop "found it advisable". The Duck asks, "Found what?", because a duck would only find a frog or a worm. The joke works because the Duck takes "it" in the wrong way, so the sentence is a clue that "advisable" means "a sensible idea".
fact: Advisable means sensible and wise to do; recommended.
fact: «It is advisable to wear a helmet» tells you that a helmet is a good idea, but it is not a strict rule.
fact: Advisable is a formal word, so you will often see it in notices and advice.
fact: The opposite is inadvisable, or not advisable: «It is inadvisable to swim straight after a big meal.»
fact: Advisable is linked to the word advice, so a good way to remember it is "something advice would tell you to do".
exercise: «It is advisable to wear a helmet when you ride a bike.» What does advisable mean? | Compulsory, you must do it by law | Expensive | Dangerous and forbidden | *Sensible and wise to do
exercise: «The doctor says it is not advisable to swim straight after a big meal.» What does not advisable mean here? | A fun game to play in the pool | *Not a sensible thing to do | Very cold water
exercise: In Alice, the Mouse says the archbishop «found it advisable». What does found it advisable mean? | found it a frog | found it a funny joke | found it a lost thing | *found it a sensible idea
test: Find and copy the word that is the opposite of advisable in the sentence «It is inadvisable to climb the wall in the rain.» | climb | advisable | *inadvisable | wall
test: Which word could replace advisable in «It is advisable to wear sunscreen on a hot day»? | late | *recommended | forbidden | silly
exam: Choose the best meaning of advisable and explain how the context helped you: «It is advisable to wear a helmet.» | a thing you can only do at night | a kind of bicycle | *sensible and wise, a good idea, not a strict rule | a strict law that you must obey
